  "slug": "lru-cache",
  "title": "Simulate an LRU Cache",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "topics": [
    "hash-maps",
    "simulation"
  ],
  "summary": "Run get/put operations on a least-recently-used cache.",
  "statement": "Simulate an LRU cache holding at most `capacity` keys. Each operation in `ops` is `\"put K V\"` (insert or\nupdate key K with value V) or `\"get K\"`. `get` returns the value, or `-1` if absent, and both operations\nmark the key as most recently used. When a put would exceed capacity, evict the least recently used key\nfirst. Return the results of the `get` operations, in order.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= capacity <= 100",
    "1 <= ops.length <= 10^4"
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "capacity = 2, ops = [\"put 1 1\", \"put 2 2\", \"get 1\", \"put 3 3\", \"get 2\", \"put 4 4\", \"get 1\", \"get 3\", \"get 4\"]",
      "output": "[1, -1, -1, 3, 4]"
    },
    {
      "input": "capacity = 1, ops = [\"put 2 1\", \"get 2\", \"put 3 2\", \"get 2\", \"get 3\"]",
      "output": "[1, -1, 2]"
    },
    {
      "input": "capacity = 2, ops = [\"put 1 1\", \"put 1 5\", \"get 1\", \"put 2 2\", \"put 3 3\", \"get 1\"]",
      "output": "[5, -1]"
    }
  ],
  "signature": {
    "method": "lruCache",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "capacity",
        "type": "int"
      },
      {
        "name": "ops",
        "type": "String[]"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "int[]"
  },
  "starter_code": "class Solution {\n    public int[] lruCache(int capacity, String[] ops) {\n        // TODO: write your solution here\n        return new int[0];\n    }\n}\n",
  "hints": [
    "You need fast lookup and fast \"move to most recent\".",
    "A hash map plus a doubly linked list does both in O(1). In Java, `LinkedHashMap` with access order is exactly this.",
    "cache = ordered map\nfor op in ops:\n    if get: if key in cache: move to end; record value else record -1\n    if put: insert/update and move to end; if size > capacity: remove the first (oldest) key",
    "Every operation is O(1). Updating an existing key also counts as a use."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(1) per op",
    "space": "O(capacity)"
  },
